      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">2. Edge Filtering: Reducing Ingestion Volume by 70%+</h2>
        <p>
          The most effective way to eliminate storage bloat is to configure <strong>Logpush Edge Filters</strong> inside your Cloudflare Dashboard or via the Cloudflare API before logs leave the network boundary.
        </p>
        <p>
          Typical high-volume noise sources include favicon requests, static CSS/JS files, and internal synthetic health probes. Here is a production-grade Logpush API filter rule configured via cURL:
        </p>

<pre is:raw class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono overflow-x-auto text-orange-400">
curl -s -X POST "https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/zones/${CF_ZONE_ID}/logpush/jobs" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer ${CF_API_TOKEN}" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "name": "filtered-http-requests-r2",
    "destination_conf": "r2://edge-telemetry-bucket/http_logs?account-id='${CF_ACCOUNT_ID}'",
    "dataset": "http_requests",
    "filter": "{\"where\":{\"and\":[{\"key\":\"ClientRequestURI\",\"operator\":\"!contains\",\"value\":\".css\"},{\"key\":\"ClientRequestURI\",\"operator\":\"!contains\",\"value\":\".jpg\"},{\"key\":\"ClientRequestURI\",\"operator\":\"!contains\",\"value\":\".png\"},{\"key\":\"ClientRequestURI\",\"operator\":\"!contains\",\"value\":\"/healthz\"}]}}",
    "logstream_spec": "edge"
  }'
</pre>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">3. ClickHouse MergeTree Table Optimization & Order By Strategy</h2>
        <p>
          ClickHouse achieves exceptional compression and multi-billion-row query speed due to sparse primary indexes and columnar run-length encoding. To maximize pruning efficiency, columns must be positioned in the <code>ORDER BY</code> tuple from lowest cardinality to highest cardinality:
        </p>

<pre is:raw class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono overflow-x-auto text-emerald-400">
-- Production ClickHouse MergeTree DDL for Cloudflare HTTP Logs
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS cloudflare_http_logs (
    EdgeStartTimestamp DateTime64(6, 'UTC') CODEC(DoubleDelta, ZSTD(3)),
    ClientRequestHost LowCardinality(String) CODEC(ZSTD(3)),
    ClientRequestMethod LowCardinality(String) CODEC(ZSTD(3)),
    EdgeResponseStatus UInt16 CODEC(T64, ZSTD(3)),
    OriginResponseStatus Nullable(UInt16) CODEC(T64, ZSTD(3)),
    EdgeColoCode LowCardinality(String) CODEC(ZSTD(3)),
    ClientCountry LowCardinality(String) CODEC(ZSTD(3)),
    ClientIP IPv6 CODEC(ZSTD(3)),
    ClientRequestURI String CODEC(ZSTD(6)),
    ClientRequestUserAgent String CODEC(ZSTD(6)),
    EdgeResponseBytes UInt64 CODEC(T64, ZSTD(3)),
    OriginResponseDurationMs UInt32 CODEC(T64, ZSTD(3)),
    RayID FixedString(16) CODEC(ZSTD(3)),
    BotScore UInt8 CODEC(T64, ZSTD(3)),
    WAFAction LowCardinality(String) CODEC(ZSTD(3))
) ENGINE = MergeTree()
PARTITION BY toDate(EdgeStartTimestamp)
ORDER BY (ClientRequestHost, EdgeResponseStatus, toDate(EdgeStartTimestamp), EdgeStartTimestamp, ClientIP)
SETTINGS index_granularity = 8192;
</pre>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">4. Ingestion Engines: ClickHouse S3Queue vs Vector Pipeline</h2>
        <p>
          There are two primary paradigms for feeding Cloudflare NDJSON batches from S3/R2 into ClickHouse:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-300">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">1. Native ClickHouse S3Queue Engine:</strong> ClickHouse polls S3/R2 directly, tracks processed files via ZooKeeper/Keeper, and ingests them without intermediary infrastructure. Highly resilient and serverless.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">2. Vector High-Throughput Stream:</strong> An external Vector daemon watches S3 object-created notifications via SQS, decompresses GZIP payloads in-memory, applies VRL enrichment (e.g. GeoIP lookups or URL normalization), and sends native bulk HTTP batches to ClickHouse.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <!-- Ingestion Benchmark Table -->
        <div class="overflow-x-auto my-6">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm border border-slate-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
            <thead class="bg-slate-900 text-white font-semibold">
