              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">5. Python Test Runner: NDJSON Batch Verification & Syntax Validation</h2>
        <p>
          Run this verification utility to validate Cloudflare Logpush NDJSON files against the expected schema before committing ingestion configs:
        </p>

<pre is:raw class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono overflow-x-auto text-orange-400">
import json
import gzip
from typing import Dict, Any

REQUIRED_FIELDS = {
    "RayID", "ClientIP", "ClientRequestHost", "ClientRequestMethod",
    "ClientRequestURI", "EdgeResponseStatus", "EdgeStartTimestamp"
}

def validate_cloudflare_ndjson_record(record_str: str) -> bool:
    try:
        data: Dict[str, Any] = json.loads(record_str)
        missing = REQUIRED_FIELDS - data.keys()
        if missing:
            print(f"Schema violation: missing fields {missing}")
            return False
        
        # Verify status code integer range
        status = data.get("EdgeResponseStatus")
        if not isinstance(status, int) or not (100 <= status <= 599):
            print(f"Invalid HTTP status: {status}")
            return False
            
        return True
    except json.JSONDecodeError as e:
        print(f"JSON decode failure: {e}")
        return False

if __name__ == "__main__":
    sample = (
        '{"RayID":"8b24ef0182a931c4","ClientIP":"198.51.100.42",'
        '"ClientRequestHost":"api.platform.io","ClientRequestMethod":"GET",'
        '"ClientRequestURI":"/v1/telemetry","EdgeResponseStatus":200,'
        '"EdgeStartTimestamp":1728118462000000000,"EdgeColoCode":"LHR",'
        '"BotScore":95,"WAFAction":"allow"}'
    )
    assert validate_cloudflare_ndjson_record(sample) is True
    print("Cloudflare NDJSON Schema: VALID")
</pre>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">6. Top 4 High-Volume Edge Logging Failure Modes & Remediation</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-300">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">1. ClickHouse "Too Many Parts" Write Backpressure:</strong> Inserting millions of rows as individual small HTTP requests causes part proliferation and throttles ClickHouse. <em>Remedy:</em> Batch inserts into chunks of at least 50,000 to 100,000 rows or use the <code>Buffer</code> table engine / S3Queue.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">2. Nanosecond Timestamp Truncation Drift:</strong> Cloudflare outputs <code>EdgeStartTimestamp</code> in epoch nanoseconds (19 digits). Casting directly to standard <code>DateTime</code> (seconds) truncates precision and destroys microsecond sorting. <em>Remedy:</em> Store timestamps as <code>DateTime64(6, 'UTC')</code> and divide raw integer nanoseconds by 1,000.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">3. S3 / R2 API Rate Limiting on Rapid File Creation:</strong> When Logpush generates thousands of small 500KB GZIP files every minute across many domains, downstream S3 <code>GET</code> workers hit S3 503 SlowDown errors. <em>Remedy:</em> Configure prefix hash partitioning or enable Cloudflare Logpush batch frequency tuning.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">4. IPv6 Formatting Incompatibilities:</strong> IPv6 addresses containing bracket encodings or leading zeros cause downstream regex parsers to fail. <em>Remedy:</em> Use ClickHouse native <code>IPv6</code> type which automatically normalizes representation to 16-byte fixed binary arrays.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 my-6">
          <div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-900/40">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-2">Can Cloudflare Logpush stream directly to ClickHouse via HTTP without S3?</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              Cloudflare Logpush requires an object store or webhook destination (e.g. Datadog, Splunk, Sumo Logic, or custom HTTPS webhook). To feed ClickHouse directly, teams configure Logpush to push to a simple serverless worker or ingest gateway that batches payloads into ClickHouse HTTP interface.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-900/40">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-2">What is the difference between Logpush and Logpull?</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              Logpull requires the client to repeatedly execute REST API calls to pull logs from Cloudflare’s buffer, which has tight rate limits and a 1-hour retention window. Logpush is fully automated push-based streaming directly to your cloud storage bucket with zero manual polling.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-900/40">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-2">How do I verify that Logpush has not dropped any logs?</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              Every Logpush batch contains a metadata header with record counts. By comparing Cloudflare Analytics GraphQL aggregated request counts against ClickHouse <code>count()</code> across 1-hour windows, engineering teams can detect and alert on any telemetry loss.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </article>

  <script is:inline>
    function updateDDL() {
      const codec = document.getElementById('ddl-codec').value;
      const partition = document.getElementById('ddl-partition').value;
      const security = document.getElementById('ddl-security').value === 'true';

      let ddl = `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS cloudflare_http_logs (\n`;
      ddl += `    EdgeStartTimestamp DateTime64(6, 'UTC') CODEC(DoubleDelta, ${codec}),\n`;
      ddl += `    ClientRequestHost LowCardinality(String) CODEC(${codec}),\n`;
      ddl += `    ClientRequestMethod LowCardinality(String) CODEC(${codec}),\n`;
      ddl += `    EdgeResponseStatus UInt16 CODEC(T64, ${codec}),\n`;
      ddl += `    OriginResponseStatus Nullable(UInt16) CODEC(T64, ${codec}),\n`;
      ddl += `    EdgeColoCode LowCardinality(String) CODEC(${codec}),\n`;
      ddl += `    ClientCountry LowCardinality(String) CODEC(${codec}),\n`;
      ddl += `    ClientIP IPv6 CODEC(${codec}),\n`;
      ddl += `    ClientRequestURI String CODEC(ZSTD(6)),\n`;
      ddl += `    EdgeResponseBytes UInt64 CODEC(T64, ${codec}),\n`;
      ddl += `    RayID FixedString(16) CODEC(${codec})`;

      if (security) {
        ddl += `,\n    BotScore UInt8 CODEC(T64, ${codec}),\n`;
        ddl += `    WAFAction LowCardinality(String) CODEC(${codec}),\n`;
        ddl += `    SecurityActions LowCardinality(String) CODEC(${codec})`;
      }

      ddl += `\n) ENGINE = MergeTree()\n`;
      ddl += `PARTITION BY ${partition}\n`;
      ddl += `ORDER BY (ClientRequestHost, EdgeResponseStatus, toDate(EdgeStartTimestamp), EdgeStartTimestamp, ClientIP)\n`;
      ddl += `SETTINGS index_granularity = 8192;`;

      document.getElementById('ddl-output').innerText = ddl;
    }

    document.getElementById('ddl-codec')?.addEventListener('change', updateDDL);
    document.getElementById('ddl-partition')?.addEventListener('change', updateDDL);
    document.getElementById('ddl-security')?.addEventListener('change', updateDDL);
    updateDDL();
  </script>
</Layout>
